 "| 744 | 2026-10-30 | **'Make your own' in place; a tool goes back to its chapter (Build CY; her 00:35).** LessonMake: each thing to make is a button (`data-make-tool`) that opens the tool itself under its name (`data-make-open`, one at a time, scrolled into view) instead of a link away. The room's Toolbox chips carry `&from=<chapter>`; the state reads it as `rc`. ToolView takes `backAlways`, its back button has `data-testid=\"tool-back\"`. toolBackCh: the chapter it was opened from, else (unless it came from the Toolbox, the Home, Practice or Today, or is locked) the tool's own chapter; the back button then says '← <chapter name>' and opens that chapter's Learn tab. From the Toolbox it still says '← Toolbox'. Test: cy774.js (all 59 rooms' Make your own open, draw and close; the chips carry from; back lands in the chapter; locked links have no back; Korean). |",
 "| 745 | 2026-10-30 | **The Prelim floor's Lesson Books, fun first (Build CZ; her 00:36 'don't wait, make it now').** As the Beginner books (CU, patches 768 and 769): one 'Guess first!' on each opener (with the page that answers it) and one challenge above every step's Remember line: listen-sing 4, tempo, rhythm, ledger lines, scales, scale playing, minor scales and signs 5 each, 39 in all. Three are 'Beat your time' with their own stopwatch ids (beat13 ledger lines' five Cs, beat14 G major's letters, beat15 the major and minor pairs); the rest '5 in a row'. Only her metaphors (walk / run-ning, the bird and the turtle, ladders, mirror twins, thumb under and 3 over) and only what the pages already teach. The scales opener's keyboard clock may shrink a little in print (min height 340) to make room. Test: cz775.js (every page fits in both languages, one guess, one challenge a step, the guess opens on screen). |",
 "| 746 | 2026-10-30 | **The Prelim checkpoint on paper (Build DA; the board's next step).** `?book=check&floor=1` (four pages) and `?book=checkkey&floor=1` (one page), as the Beginner ones (CX): two parts of each Prelim room's check-up on paper, new items on the checkpoint route only (`if (CKP) Object.assign(...)` after STM_CHK, SRH_CHK, SSC_CHK, SP_WB, MS_WB and SGN_CHK; llChkData's sky and sea). Parts: Ear Training, Prelim A and B (new, the teacher plays: higher or lower with the bird and the turtle; same or different rhythm; LsCkpPaper and LsCkpKey), tempo B F, rhythm C E, ledger lines B C, scales A C, scale playing A C, minor scales B D, signs A B (picked so the pages fit in chapter order: 14 to 16, 17 and 18, 19 and 20, 21 with the rooms-to-visit list). skgTcAns carries data-sec, so the signs key can pick its parts. The key says 'steps 1 and 3 (Lesson Book pages 2 and 4)' for a part with two; a checkpoint of more than seven rooms says about 20 minutes. Tests: da776.js (FLOORS=0a,0b,1: pages, overflow, two parts a room, the key's answers), shelf776.js (three checkpoint rows). |",
 "| 747 | 2026-10-30 | **The Grade 1 floor's Lesson Books, fun first (Build DB; the board's next step).** As CZ: one 'Guess first!' on each opener and one challenge above every step's Remember line: listen-write 3, accidentals, key signatures, terms, six-eight, intervals, chords and form 5 each, 38 in all; four 'Beat your time' with stopwatch ids beat16 to beat19 (accidentals' high F sharp and low F, key signatures' every F sharp, intervals above G, chords' triads on every white key). Five openers (key signatures, terms, intervals, chords, form) and the terms book's page 2 in Korean were full: their pictures' print height (LbPic or stack minimum) is lower in print only, the frame fitting the drawing to the room left; the screen is unchanged. The Form book's check-up page said 'on its page (1 to 5)': now 2 to 6, as its steps are. Test: cz775.js with the 16 Prelim and Grade 1 ids. |",
 "| 748 | 2026-10-30 | **The Grade 1 checkpoint on paper (Build DC).** `?book=check&floor=2` (four pages) and `?book=checkkey&floor=2` (one page), as DA. Parts, picked so the pages fit in chapter order (22 and 23, 24 and 25, 26 and 27, 28 and 29 with the rooms-to-visit list): Ear Training, Grade 1 A and B (new, the teacher plays: home or not home; in two or in three; LwCkpPaper, LwCkpKey), accidentals A E, key signatures A B, terms A C, six-eight A C, intervals B C, chords B C, form A B. New items on the checkpoint route (SAC_CHK signs and circ, SKG_CHK name and which, TMX_CHK mean and pick, E8_WB.chk len and see in a new order, IVX_CHK above and mh, CHX_CHK draw and mm, FMX_CHK sd and bt); every answer is computed from the data. The key says 'steps 1 to 5' too. Test: dc778.js (FLOORS=0a,0b,1,2), shelf776.js with N=4. |",
